Countable nouns have a singular and <sup>1<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_0\"><\/gap> form: <em>egg \u2013 eggs<\/em>.<\/p><p>\u2022 Uncountable nouns do not have a <sup>2<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_1\"><\/gap> form: <em>juice \u2013 juice<\/em>.<\/p><p>\u2022 We use <em>a \/ an<\/em> with countable nouns. Use <sup>3<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_2\"><\/gap> if the noun begins with a vowel sound: <em>a banana<\/em> \u2013 <em>an apple<\/em>.<\/p><p>\u2022 We use <sup>4<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_3\"><\/gap> and <sup>5<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_4\"><\/gap> with uncountable nouns and plural countable nouns: <em>There are some eggs<\/em> \u2013 <em>There isn\u2019t any cereal<\/em>.<\/p><p>\u2022 We usually use <sup>6<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_5\"><\/gap> in questions and negatives, and <sup>7<\/sup> <gap id=\"gap_6\"><\/gap> in affirmative sentences: <em>Do we have any bread? Yes, we have some bread<\/em>.<\/p>"],"configs":[{"correctAnswer":"plural","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_0","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_3\/p38_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"plural","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_1","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_3\/p38_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"an","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_2","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_3\/p38_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"some","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_3","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_3\/p38_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"any","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_4","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_3\/p38_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"some","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"gap_5","type":"gap","exerciseUrl":"https:\/\/exercise-editor.helbling.com\/files\/potential_a2\/SB\/unit_3\/p38_ex1ab\/"},{"correctAnswer":"any","additionalAnswers":[],"id":"ga